"<p>Nitrobase provides two automated installation methods that produce the exact same layout (<code>/opt/nitrobase</code> with <code>.env</code> and <code>docker-compose.prod.yml</code>, compose project <code>nitrobase</code>, container <code>nitrobase_app</code>), so in-panel upgrades work identically for both.</p>\n<h2>Option 1: Install Script (Ubuntu or Debian VPS)</h2>\n<p>Connect to a fresh <strong>Ubuntu or Debian</strong> VPS (<code>amd64</code> or <code>arm64</code>) and run:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">curl</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -fsSL</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> https://nitrobase.app/install.sh</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> |</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> sudo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> bash</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>If <code>nitrobase.app</code> is unreachable, use the copy in the repository:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">curl</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -fsSL</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/AydenGroup/nitrobase/main/scripts/install.sh</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> |</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> sudo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> bash</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Each GitHub release also attaches its versioned <code>install.sh</code>, and any running Nitrobase panel serves its own version at <code>https://&#x3C;panel>/api/install.sh</code>.</p>\n<h2>Option 2: Docker Installer Image (Any OS with Docker)</h2>\n<p>On any machine with Docker (<code>amd64</code> or <code>arm64</code>), run the official installer image (Nitrobase is currently in beta, so <code>:beta</code> tracks the newest pre-release; <code>:latest</code> will track stable releases once published):</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">docker</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> run</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> --rm</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -it</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  -v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  -v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> /opt/nitrobase:/opt/nitrobase</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">  ghcr.io/aydengroup/nitrobase-installer:beta</span></span></code></pre>\n<div class=\"docCallout docCallout-note\"><div class=\"docCalloutHeader\"><span class=\"docCalloutBadge\">NOTE</span><span class=\"docCalloutTitle\">Matching Mount Paths</span></div><div class=\"docCalloutContent\">\n<p>The install directory mount (<code>-v /opt/nitrobase:/opt/nitrobase</code>) <strong>must use the exact same path on both sides</strong> so Docker resolves the compose project folder on the host and in-panel upgrades can mount it later. For a custom folder, change both sides and pass <code>--dir</code>:\n<code>-v /srv/nitrobase:/srv/nitrobase ... --dir /srv/nitrobase</code>.</p>\n</div></div>\n<p>Both images are also mirrored on Docker Hub as <code>jimmyphong/nitrobase</code> and <code>jimmyphong/nitrobase-installer</code>, while GHCR (<code>ghcr.io/aydengroup/nitrobase</code>) remains the default source.</p>\n<h3>Docker Desktop (macOS / Windows)</h3>\n<p>On macOS, <code>/opt</code> is not shared by Docker Desktop by default. Install under <code>$HOME/nitrobase</code> instead (on Windows, run from a WSL 2 shell):</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">docker</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> run</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> --rm</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -it</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  -v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">  -v</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">$HOME</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">/nitrobase:</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">$HOME</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">/nitrobase\"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> \\</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">  ghcr.io/aydengroup/nitrobase-installer:beta</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> --dir</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> \"</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\">$HOME</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\">/nitrobase\"</span></span></code></pre>\n<p>Note that on Docker Desktop, the <em>Localhost</em> server is Docker's Linux VM rather than your host OS.</p>\n<h2>What the Installer Does</h2>\n<p>The installer is <strong>idempotent</strong>—re-running it keeps your secrets and database intact:</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Preflight checks:</strong> Verifies root access, OS (<code>ubuntu</code>/<code>debian</code> on host), CPU, RAM (warns below ~1.8 GB), disk (warns below 5 GB, stops below 2 GB), and ports. Installs Docker CE from Docker's official apt repository if missing (asks first unless <code>--yes</code> is passed).</li>\n<li><strong>Secret generation:</strong> Creates <code>/opt/nitrobase/.env</code> with <code>0600</code> permissions containing generated <code>ENCRYPTION_KEY</code>, <code>SESSION_SECRET</code>, and <code>POSTGRES_PASSWORD</code>.</li>\n<li><strong>One-time setup token:</strong> Generates a 32-character hex <code>SETUP_TOKEN</code> and prints it to your terminal so nobody else can claim a fresh panel before you.</li>\n<li><strong>Release channel:</strong> When installing a pre-release and <code>.env</code> has no <code>RELEASE_CHANNEL</code>, sets <code>RELEASE_CHANNEL=prerelease</code> so the panel offers subsequent pre-releases.</li>\n<li><strong>Starts services:</strong> Downloads <code>docker-compose.prod.yml</code>, starts <code>nitrobase_postgres</code> and <code>nitrobase_app</code>, waits until <code>/api/health</code> is healthy (up to 300s), and prints next steps.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2>Installer Options</h2>\n<p>Pass options after <code>sudo bash -s --</code> (script) or after the image name (Docker installer):</p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<table><thead><tr><th align=\"left\">Option</th><th align=\"left\">Description</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td align=\"left\"><code>--version &#x3C;v></code></td><td align=\"left\">Specific release to install (e.g. <code>0.1.0-beta.9</code>). Re-run to change versions.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><code>--dir &#x3C;path></code></td><td align=\"left\">Install directory (default <code>/opt/nitrobase</code>).</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><code>--panel-bind &#x3C;addr:port></code></td><td align=\"left\">Host bind address (default <code>0.0.0.0:3000</code>; <code>127.0.0.1:3000</code> when <code>--domain</code> is set).</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><code>--domain &#x3C;host></code></td><td align=\"left\">Serve the panel over HTTPS via Traefik + Let's Encrypt; sets <code>APP_URL</code> and <code>TRUST_PROXY=true</code>.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><code>--repo &#x3C;owner/name></code></td><td align=\"left\">Install releases from a fork (default <code>AydenGroup/nitrobase</code>). For Gitea/Forgejo, also pass <code>--api-url</code> and <code>--raw-url</code>.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><code>--image &#x3C;name></code> / <code>--compose-url &#x3C;url></code></td><td align=\"left\">Override the panel image or compose file URL.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><code>--yes</code></td><td align=\"left\">Do not prompt before installing Docker.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><code>--skip-resource-check</code></td><td align=\"left\">Bypass RAM and disk minimums on small test machines.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><code>--uninstall</code></td><td align=\"left\">Stop and remove containers while keeping data volumes and <code>.env</code>.</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><code>--uninstall --purge</code></td><td align=\"left\">Also delete data volumes and empty the install folder (requires typing <code>purge &#x3C;dir></code>, or setting <code>-e NITROBASE_PURGE_CONFIRM=\"purge &#x3C;dir>\"</code> non-interactively).</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\"><code>--print-config</code> / <code>--help</code></td><td align=\"left\">Print resolved configuration without making changes, or show help.</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<h2>Adding Swap on a Small VPS</h2>\n<p>On a 1–2 GB VPS, adding a 2 GB swap file prevents sudden OOM container kills:</p>\n<pre class=\"shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark\" style=\"--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark:#e1e4e8;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;--shiki-dark-bg:#24292e\" tabindex=\"0\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">sudo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> fallocate</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -l</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> 2G</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> /swapfile</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> &#x26;&#x26; </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">sudo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> chmod</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> 600</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> /swapfile</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> &#x26;&#x26; </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">sudo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> mkswap</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> /swapfile</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#24292E;--shiki-dark:#E1E4E8\"> &#x26;&#x26; </span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\">sudo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> swapon</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> /swapfile</span></span>\n<span class=\"line\"><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\">echo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> '/swapfile none swap sw 0 0'</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#D73A49;--shiki-dark:#F97583\"> |</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#B392F0\"> sudo</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> tee</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#79B8FF\"> -a</span><span style=\"--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#9ECBFF\"> /etc/fstab</span></span></code></pre>\n<h2>Accessing Your Panel</h2>\n<p>Once healthy, open <code>http://&#x3C;server-ip>:3000</code> (or tunnel over SSH first: <code>ssh -L 3000:localhost:3000 root@&#x3C;server-ip></code>) and proceed to <strong>First-Run Setup</strong>.</p>"